course: dictionary
lesson: 9165
title: Snowman in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word, and they often give you clues to its meaning. «When it snows, Sashko builds a snowman.» The words snows and builds tell you a snowman is something you make out of snow.
explain: Check your guess by swapping your meaning into the sentence. «Sashko builds a figure of a person made of snow.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Some sentences use a word to describe something else. «Arrokoth is a Kuiper belt object shaped like a snowman.» Here the word tells you the shape of the object, so you can picture it as two or three round lumps stacked up.
fact: A snowman is a figure of a person made of snow.
fact: A snowman is usually two or three big snowballs stacked on top of each other.
fact: A snowman often has a face of stones or coal and a carrot nose.
fact: «Snowman» is a noun, and its plural is «snowmen».
fact: «The snowman melted» means the snow turned to water when the temperature rose above 0 °C.
fact: «Snizhky» means snowballs in Ukrainian, and «snIhovyk» means snowman.
exercise: «When it snows, Sashko builds a snowman.» What is a snowman? | A tall tree covered in ice | A sled for going down hills | *A figure of a person made of snow | A warm coat made of wool
exercise: «The snowman melted.» What happened to the snowman? | It froze solid and stayed the same | *It turned to water because it got warm | It grows bigger every day | It turned into a tree
exercise: «Il neige» means "It's snowing". What does «un bonhomme de neige» mean? | *A snowman | A coat | Snow | A snowball fight
test: «Insulation slows heat flow, so a coat wrapped round a snowman makes it last longer.» What does this sentence suggest? | Coats are only for people | A snowman needs a hat to see | *A coat helps a snowman last longer | A coat makes a snowman melt faster
test: What is the plural of snowman? | *snowmen | snowmens | snowman's | snowmans
exam: Which sentence uses snowman to describe a shape rather than a real snowman? | «Hraimo v snizhky!» | «Sashko builds a snowman.» | *«Arrokoth is a Kuiper belt object shaped like a snowman.» | «The snowman melted.»
